# AI composition studio

Read and follow `studio-tools/AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md` before creating or
revising a composition, publishing, or changing the studio's tools or viewer.

- Work only in `music/ai-compositions/`, `docs/compositions/`, `docs/studio/`
  and `studio-tools/`. Do not modify anything else in this repository.
- Use `studio-tools/bin/studio` for every change to the archive and the
  published files: `new` or `stage`, `prompt`, `run`, `render`, `accept`,
  `publish`. Never edit `version-NNNN/` directories, accepted prompts or
  manifests by hand.
- Save the user's prompt verbatim with `studio prompt` before doing the work.
- The composition is one complete `.csd`. P-fields: p1 instrument, p2 time,
  p3 duration, p4 MIDI key, p5 MIDI velocity, p6 depth, p7 pan, p8 height,
  p9 phase, p10 pitch-class set, p11 homogeneity.
- With CsoundAC, use only methods that exist; see
  `studio-tools/docs/csound-conventions.md`. Create events with all eleven
  arguments.
- Do not pass `;` comment lines to `scoreline` or `scorelinei`.
- Commit only the studio's directories; never `git add -A`. Do not push,
  merge or deploy unless asked.
- Report actual command output; do not claim unverified results.
